    {
      "id": "msg-2",
      "role": "assistant",
      "text": "**The case still matches revision 1.2.** Its openings are cut exactly where the 1.2 board puts them: `opening_Q4` over Q4 at (1.90, 123.71) and `opening_U2` over U2 at (15.80, 102.81). The outline, mounting holes `H1`/`H2` and tallest parts are the same in both revisions. That's why the 67 checks covering walls, draft, inserts, clearance and height all pass.\n\n**Against revision 2.0, 8 checks fail, caused by 4 board changes:**\n\n| Component | What changed in 2.0 | Failing checks (all on the lid) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Q4` light sensor | Moved to (1.08, 120.74) and rotated 90° | Its window is off by 2.82 mm against ±0.2 mm, and 9.1 mm³ of lid covers the sensor |\n| `U2` humidity sensor | Moved to (17.08, 97.37) | Its vent is off by 5.67 mm against ±0.2 mm, and 18.1 mm³ of lid covers the sensor |\n| `SW1` button | New, at (6.92, 103.21) | No opening; 35.3 mm³ of lid in the way |\n| `RST1` button | New, at (15.30, 103.21) | No opening, and the old U2 vent holes sit over it; 19.3 mm³ in the way |\n\n**Other results:**\n- **Height:** the case is exactly at the 15.1 mm limit, with no margin, because that limit was taken from this case.\n- **Fit to an object:** doesn't apply, since the case isn't built around an object.\n- **Not tested:** strength, drop and heat need a review by hand.\n\nI haven't changed anything. To update the case for 2.0, I would move the `opening_Q4` window to the new Q4 position and turn it 90°, move the `opening_U2` vent to the new U2 position, and add button openings for `SW1` and `RST1`. Should I go ahead?",
      "created_at": "2026-11-18T10:44:21.700285Z",
      "model": null,
      "effort": null,
      "mode": null,
      "selection": null,
      "answer": null,
